<http://data.silknow.org/object/2e2a7ca8-6afe-33f8-b2ea-674a7b91f388>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A man's waistcoat of silk with a standing collar of 4.5 cm, curving front and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  There is a pocket and shaped pocket flap on each front.  The fronts are made of cream silk striped with brown and pale grey silk in a lozenge pattern, bordered with stripes of silver strip.  The back is made of cream worsted twill; the waistcoat lined with bleached fustian; the skirts lined and fronts faced with ivory silk twill.  The front edges, hem, collar and pocket flaps are edged with a 7 cm wide ribbon of white silk and silver strip.  There are 13 worked buttonholes along the right front and 13 corresponding buttons covered with a woven silver fabric on the right front, and three below each pocket."@en , "A man's waistcoat, British, 1780-85, of cream silk striped with brown and silver."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/66ee933f-1140-3d77-be47-1c34fbcc7e20> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1b8f23e6-ffdc-34fc-b686-5b659531bac3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/aaebc370-2a1c-3d97-ae24-e3a7dd4600b1> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/74e1f0df-a117-31c3-ad1a-c57f5ea046a4> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/3ba46da1-de28-3024-9856-fbadf6fe23b4> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/db0cdce9-9b51-389e-821f-f4ca168fb3f4> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "A man's waistcoat of silk with a standing collar of 4.5 cm, curving front and skirts reaching to the top of the thigh.  There is a pocket and shaped pocket flap on each front.  The fronts are made of cream silk striped with brown and pale grey silk in a lozenge pattern, bordered with stripes of silver strip.  The back is made of cream worsted twill; the waistcoat lined with bleached fustian; the skirts lined and fronts faced with ivory silk twill.  The front edges, hem, collar and pocket flaps are edged with a 7 cm wide ribbon of white silk and silver strip.  There are 13 worked buttonholes along the right front and 13 corresponding buttons covered with a woven silver fabric on the right front, and three below each pocket."@en , "A man's waistcoat, British, 1780-85, of cream silk striped with brown and silver."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/2e2a7ca8-6afe-33f8-b2ea-674a7b91f388/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/2e2a7ca8-6afe-33f8-b2ea-674a7b91f388/dimension/2> ;
